-- The Network and Information Systems Regulations 2018 (S.I. 2018/506).
-- Regulations 1, 3(2), 8 (as a fact), 11, 12(1)-(9), 17(1)-(2) and 18(1), (2), (5)-(7):
-- who is in scope, which incidents must be notified, to whom, by when, and the
-- penalty ceiling for failing to notify.
--
-- DRAFT. Not for use as advice. No domain expert and no lawyer qualified in the law of
-- any part of the United Kingdom has read this against the source.
-- The source is an AID (the Lex API's re-serving of legislation.gov.uk data); it was
-- NOT checked against the official text. These are cyber-security regulations, not an
-- AI law; nothing here says an AI service is within them.
--
-- Seat: a company providing an AI model service. Source:
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2018-506.txt; `src:N` is line N.
-- Target compiler: main. Forks F1 to F12 are in NOTES.md.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nis-domain`

§ `Regulation 1 -- Am I within the Regulations?`

-- src:85 | Section 1) **Citation, commencement, interpretation and application**
-- src:87 | 1) These Regulations may be cited as the Network and Information Systems Regulations 2018 and come into force on 10th May 2018.
-- src:88 | 2) In these Regulations—
-- src:89 | - “cloud computing service” means a digital service that enables access to a scalable and elastic pool of shareable computing resources;
-- src:94 | - “digital service” means a service within the meaning of point (b) of Article 1(1) of Directive 2015/1535 which is of any the following kinds— online marketplace;online search engine;cloud computing service;
-- src:95 | - “digital service provider” means any person who provides a digital service;
-- src:106 | - “online marketplace” means a digital service that allows consumers and/or traders as respectively defined in point (a) and in point (b) of Article 4(1) of Directive 2013/11 to conclude online sales or service contracts with traders either on the online marketplace's website or on a trader's website that uses computing services provided by the online marketplace;
-- src:107 | - “online search engine” means a digital service that allows users to perform searches of, in principle, all websites or websites in a particular language on the basis of a query on any subject in the form of a keyword, phrase or other input, and returns links in which information related to the requested content can be found;
-- The three kinds are the provider's to state, with "I cannot say" allowed (fork F1):
-- the text says nothing about AI models or APIs. "Directive 2015/1535" point (b) of
-- Article 1(1) is not deposited, so whether the service is an information society
-- service is asked as a fact.
@ref regulation 1(2), "digital service", "cloud computing service", "online marketplace", "online search engine" (src:85-107)
DECLARE `is my service a digital service` IS ONE OF
    `my service is a digital service`
    `my service is not a digital service`
    `my service is a digital service only if it is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`

@ref regulation 1(2) (src:89-107)
GIVEN a IS A `my answer to a classification`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the answer is yes` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `yes, it is` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@ref regulation 1(2) (src:89-107)
GIVEN a IS A `my answer to a classification`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the answer is not known` a MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN `I cannot say` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@ref regulation 1(2), "digital service" (src:94)
GIVEN p IS A `the provider as it describes itself`
GIVETH A `is my service a digital service`
`whether my service is a digital service` p MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT p's `my service is an information society service within Article 1(1)(b) of Directive 2015/1535`)
            THEN `my service is not a digital service`
        IF     `the answer is yes` (p's `is my service a cloud computing service`)
            OR `the answer is yes` (p's `is my service an online search engine`)
            OR `the answer is yes` (p's `is my service an online marketplace`)
            THEN `my service is a digital service`
        IF     `the answer is not known` (p's `is my service a cloud computing service`)
            OR `the answer is not known` (p's `is my service an online search engine`)
            OR `the answer is not known` (p's `is my service an online marketplace`)
            THEN `my service is a digital service only if it is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`
        OTHERWISE `my service is not a digital service`

-- src:110 | - “representative” means any natural or legal person established in the United Kingdom who is able to act on behalf of a digital service provider established outside the United Kingdom with regard to its obligations under these Regulations; and
-- src:112 | 3) In these Regulations a reference to—
-- src:116 | d) the “designated competent authority for an OES” is a reference to the competent authority that is designated under regulation 3(1) for the subsector in relation to which that OES provides an essential service;
-- src:117 | e) a “relevant digital service provider” (“RDSP”) is a reference to a person who provides a digital service in the United Kingdom and satisfies the following conditions—
-- src:118 | i) the head office for that provider is in the United Kingdom or that provider has nominated a representative who is established in the United Kingdom;
-- src:119 | ii) the provider is not a micro or small enterprise as defined in Commission Recommendation 2003/361/EC ;
-- Read literally, a provider with its head office outside the United Kingdom that has
-- NOT nominated a UK representative is not an RDSP at all (fork F7), even though
-- regulation 14A (deferred) requires it to nominate one.
@ref regulation 1(3)(e) (src:110-119)
DECLARE `am I an RDSP` IS ONE OF
    `I am an RDSP`
    `I am not an RDSP`
    `I am an RDSP only if my service is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`

@ref regulation 1(3)(e) (src:117-119)
GIVEN p IS A `the provider as it describes itself`
GIVETH A `am I an RDSP`
`whether I am an RDSP` p MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT p's `I provide the service in the United Kingdom`)
            THEN `I am not an RDSP`
        IF (NOT (p's `my head office is in the United Kingdom` OR p's `I have nominated a representative established in the United Kingdom`))
            THEN `I am not an RDSP`
        IF p's `I am a micro or small enterprise as defined in Commission Recommendation 2003/361/EC`
            THEN `I am not an RDSP`
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `whether my service is a digital service` p
            WHEN `my service is a digital service` THEN `I am an RDSP`
            WHEN `my service is not a digital service` THEN `I am not an RDSP`
            WHEN `my service is a digital service only if it is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`
                THEN `I am an RDSP only if my service is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`

-- src:105 | - “OES” (“operator of an essential service”) means a person who is deemed to be designated as an operator of an essential service under regulation 8(1) or (2A) or is designated as an operator of an essential service under regulation 8(3);
-- src:231 | 1) If a person provides an essential service of a kind referred to in ... Schedule 2 and that service—
-- src:232 | a) relies on network and information systems; and
-- src:233 | b) satisfies a threshold requirement described for that kind of essential service, that person is deemed to be designated as an OES for the subsector that is specified with respect to that essential service in that Schedule.
-- src:237 | 3) Even if a person does not meet the threshold requirement mentioned in paragraph (1)(b), a competent authority may designate that person as an OES for the subsector in relation to which that competent authority is designated under regulation 3(1), if the following conditions are met—
-- Schedule 2's sector thresholds are deferred, so being an OES is asked as a fact.
@ref regulation 1(2), "OES"; regulation 8(1) and (3) (src:105, src:231-237)
GIVEN p IS A `the provider as it describes itself`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`I am an OES` p MEANS
    p's `I am an OES, designated or deemed designated under regulation 8`

@ref regulation 1(2), "OES" (src:105); regulation 1(3)(e), quoted above
DECLARE `do the Regulations apply to me` IS ONE OF
    `yes, as an OES and as an RDSP`
    `yes, as an OES; and as an RDSP too if my service is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`
    `yes, as an OES only`
    `yes, as an RDSP only`
    `only as an RDSP, and only if my service is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`
    `no: I am neither an OES nor an RDSP`

@ref regulation 1(2), "OES" (src:105); regulation 1(3)(e), quoted above
GIVEN p IS A `the provider as it describes itself`
GIVETH A `do the Regulations apply to me`
`whether the Regulations apply to me` p MEANS
    IF `I am an OES` p
        THEN CONSIDER `whether I am an RDSP` p
             WHEN `I am an RDSP` THEN `yes, as an OES and as an RDSP`
             WHEN `I am not an RDSP` THEN `yes, as an OES only`
             WHEN `I am an RDSP only if my service is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`
                 THEN `yes, as an OES; and as an RDSP too if my service is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`
        ELSE CONSIDER `whether I am an RDSP` p
             WHEN `I am an RDSP` THEN `yes, as an RDSP only`
             WHEN `I am not an RDSP` THEN `no: I am neither an OES nor an RDSP`
             WHEN `I am an RDSP only if my service is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`
                 THEN `only as an RDSP, and only if my service is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`

§ `Regulation 11 -- An OES's duty to notify a NIS incident`

-- src:103 | - “incident” means any event having an actual adverse effect on the security of network and information systems;
-- src:283 | Section 11) **The duty to notify incidents**
-- src:285 | 1) An OES must notify the designated competent authority for the OES in writing about any incident which has a significant impact on the continuity of the essential service which that OES provides (“a network and information systems (“NIS”) incident”).
-- src:286 | 2) In order to determine the significance of the impact of an incident an OES must have regard to the following factors—
-- src:287 | a) the number of users affected by the disruption of the essential service;
-- src:288 | b) the duration of the incident; and
-- src:289 | c) the geographical area affected by the incident.
-- The significance is the OES's own determination, having regard to (2)(a)-(c); it is
-- asked as a fact.
@ref regulation 1(2), "incident"; regulation 11(1) and (2) (src:103, src:283-289)
GIVEN p IS A `the provider as it describes itself`, e IS A `the event as I know it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I must notify my designated competent authority under regulation 11(1)` p e IF
        `I am an OES` p
    AND e's `the event had an actual adverse effect on the security of network and information systems`
    AND e's `the incident had a significant impact on the continuity of my essential service`

-- src:290 | 3) The notification mentioned in paragraph (1) must—
-- src:291 | a) provide the following—
-- src:292 | i) the operator's name and the essential services it provides;
-- src:293 | ii) the time the NIS incident occurred;
-- src:294 | iii) the duration of the NIS incident;
-- src:295 | iv) information concerning the nature and impact of the NIS incident;
-- src:296 | v) information concerning any, or any likely, cross-border impact of the NIS incident; and
-- src:297 | vi) any other information that may be helpful to the competent authority; and
-- src:298 | b) be provided to the competent authority—
-- src:299 | i) without undue delay and in any event no later than 72 hours after the operator is aware that a NIS incident has occurred; and
-- src:300 | ii) in such form and manner as the competent authority determines.
-- src:301 | 4) The information to be provided by an OES under paragraph (3)(a) is limited to information which may reasonably be expected to be within the knowledge of that OES.
-- The content list (3)(a) and the form (3)(b)(ii) are inert here: the seat's penalty
-- question asks whether the required information was given, as a fact.
-- The 72-hour clock runs from awareness "that a NIS incident has occurred", that is, an
-- incident with a significant impact (fork F2), and is computed in the next section.

§ `Regulation 12 -- An RDSP's duty to notify an incident`

-- src:317 | Section 12) **Relevant digital service providers**
-- src:319 | 1) A RDSP must identify and take appropriate and proportionate measures to manage the risks posed to the security of network and information systems on which it relies to provide, within the United Kingdom , the following services—
-- src:320 | a) online marketplace;
-- src:321 | b) online search engine; or
-- src:322 | c) cloud computing service.
-- src:332 | 3) A RDSP must notify the Information Commission in writing about any incident having a substantial impact on the provision of any of the digital services mentioned in paragraph (1) that it provides.
-- src:333 | 4) The requirement to notify in paragraph (3) applies only if the RDSP has access to information which enables it to assess whether the impact of an incident is substantial.
-- src:344 | 7) In order to determine whether the impact of an incident is substantial the RDSP must—
-- src:345 | a) take into account the following parameters, as specified in Article 3 of EU Regulation 2018/151—
-- src:346 | i) the number of users affected by the incident and, in particular, the users relying on the digital service for the provision of their own services;
-- src:347 | ii) the duration of the incident;
-- src:348 | iii) the geographical area affected by the incident;
-- src:349 | iv) the extent of the disruption to the functioning of the service;
-- src:350 | v) the extent of the impact on economic and societal activities; and
-- src:351 | b) have regard to any relevant guidance published by the Information Commission .
-- "Substantial" is the RDSP's own determination under (7), asked as a fact.
-- EU Regulation 2018/151, as it stands in the UK (an aid text, eur-2018-151.txt), gives
-- the parameters of (7)(a) and, in this deposited aid text, NO threshold: its Article 4
-- is shown omitted (whether the official text has one was not checked).
-- src:eur-2018-151:1 | Article 3) **Parameters to be taken into account to determine whether the impact of an incident is substantial**
-- src:eur-2018-151:3 | 1) With regard to the number of users affected by an incident, in particular users relying on the service for the provision of their own services referred to in regulation 12(7)(a)(i) of the NIS Regulations , the RDSP shall be in a position to estimate either of the following:
-- src:eur-2018-151:4 | a) the number of affected natural and legal persons with whom a contract for the provision of the service has been concluded; or
-- src:eur-2018-151:5 | b) the number of affected users having used the service based in particular on previous traffic data.
-- src:eur-2018-151:6 | 2) The duration of an incident referred to in regulation 12(7)(a)(ii) of the NIS Regulations means the time period from the disruption of the proper provision of the service in terms of availability, authenticity, integrity or confidentiality until the time of recovery.
-- src:eur-2018-151:7 | 3) As far as the geographical spread with regard to the area affected by the incident referred to in regulation 12(7)(a)(iii) of the NIS Regulations is concerned, the RDSP shall be in a position to identify whether the incident affects the provision of its services in specific areas of the United Kingdom .
-- src:eur-2018-151:8 | 4) The extent of disruption of the functioning of the service referred to in regulation 12(7)(a)(iv) of the NIS Regulations shall be measured as regards one or more of the following characteristics impaired by an incident: the availability, authenticity, integrity or confidentiality of data or related services.
-- src:eur-2018-151:9 | 5) With regard to the extent of the impact on economic and societal activities referred to in regulation 12(7)(a)(v) of the NIS Regulations , the RDSP shall be able to conclude, based on indications such as the nature of his contractual relations with the customer or, where appropriate, the potential number of affected users, whether the incident has caused significant material or non-material losses for the users such as in relation to health, safety or damage to property.
-- src:eur-2018-151:10 | 6) For the purpose of paragraph 1, 2, 3, 4 and 5, the RDSPs shall not be required to collect additional information to which they do not have access.
-- src:eur-2018-151:12 | Article 4) **Substantial impact of an incident**
-- (line 13, Article 4's body, is a row of dots: omitted in the deposited aid text.)
@ref regulation 12(1), (3), (4) and (7) (src:317-351); EU Regulation 2018/151, Articles 3 and 4 (src:eur-2018-151:1-12)
DECLARE `does an RDSP duty apply` IS ONE OF
    `the duty applies`
    `the duty does not apply`
    `the duty applies only if my service is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`

@ref regulation 12(3) and (4), quoted above
GIVEN p IS A `the provider as it describes itself`, e IS A `the event as I know it`
GIVETH A `does an RDSP duty apply`
`whether I must notify the Information Commission under regulation 12(3)` p e MEANS
    IF     e's `the event had an actual adverse effect on the security of network and information systems`
       AND e's `the incident had a substantial impact on the provision of a digital service I provide`
       AND e's `I have access to information that enables me to assess whether the impact is substantial`
        THEN CONSIDER `whether I am an RDSP` p
             WHEN `I am an RDSP` THEN `the duty applies`
             WHEN `I am not an RDSP` THEN `the duty does not apply`
             WHEN `I am an RDSP only if my service is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`
                 THEN `the duty applies only if my service is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`
        ELSE `the duty does not apply`

-- src:353 | 9) If an OES is reliant on a RDSP to provide an essential service, the operator must notify the designated competent authority for the OES in writing in relation to it about any significant impact on the continuity of the service it provides caused by an incident affecting the RDSP without undue delay .
@ref regulation 12(9) (src:353)
GIVEN p IS A `the provider as it describes itself`, e IS A `the event as I know it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I must notify my designated competent authority under regulation 12(9)` p e IF
        `I am an OES` p
    AND e's `an incident affecting an RDSP I rely on had a significant impact on the continuity of my essential service`

§ `Regulation 14A -- Must I nominate a UK representative?`

-- src:1 | Section 14A) **Representatives of digital service providers established outside the United Kingdom**
-- src:3 | 1) This regulation applies to any digital service provider which—
-- src:4 | a) has its head office outside the United Kingdom, but which offers digital services within the United Kingdom; and
-- src:5 | b) is not a small or micro enterprise as defined in Commission Recommendation 2003/361/EC.
-- src:6 | 2) The digital service provider must—
-- src:7 | a) nominate in writing a representative in the United Kingdom; and
-- src:8 | b) notify the Information Commission of the name and contact details of that representative.
-- "Offers digital services within the United Kingdom" (14A(1)(a)) is asked with the same
-- fact as "provides a digital service in the United Kingdom" (1(3)(e)).
-- The answer does not depend on whether a representative has already been nominated:
-- the duty is the same. Until one is nominated, the provider is not an RDSP (F7).
@ref regulation 14A(1) and (2) (src:1-8)
DECLARE `must I nominate a UK representative` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I must nominate a UK representative in writing and notify the Information Commission of its name and contact details`
    `no: regulation 14A does not apply to me`
    `only if my service is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`

@ref regulation 14A(1) and (2) (src:3-8)
GIVEN p IS A `the provider as it describes itself`
GIVETH A `must I nominate a UK representative`
`whether I must nominate a UK representative` p MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF p's `my head office is in the United Kingdom`
            THEN `no: regulation 14A does not apply to me`
        IF (NOT p's `I provide the service in the United Kingdom`)
            THEN `no: regulation 14A does not apply to me`
        IF p's `I am a micro or small enterprise as defined in Commission Recommendation 2003/361/EC`
            THEN `no: regulation 14A does not apply to me`
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `whether my service is a digital service` p
            WHEN `my service is a digital service`
                THEN `yes: I must nominate a UK representative in writing and notify the Information Commission of its name and contact details`
            WHEN `my service is not a digital service` THEN `no: regulation 14A does not apply to me`
            WHEN `my service is a digital service only if it is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`
                THEN `only if my service is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`

-- The time for nominating is NOT computed (fork F13):
-- src:9 | 3) The digital service provider must comply with paragraph (2)—
-- src:10 | a) in the case of a provider which is offering digital services within the United Kingdom on the coming into force date of these regulations, within three months of the date on which these regulations come into force; or
-- src:11 | b) in any other case, within three months of the provider first offering digital services in the United Kingdom.
-- "these regulations" in (a) may be these Regulations (in force 10 May 2018, reg 1(1)) or
-- the instrument that inserted 14A (S.I. 2019/1444 by Lex's amendment index; not read),
-- and the text does not say how "within three months" is counted.
-- src:12 | 4) The Information Commission or GCHQ may contact the representative instead of or in addition to the digital service provider for the purposes of ensuring compliance with these Regulations.
-- src:13 | 5) A nomination under paragraph (1) is without prejudice to any legal action which could be initiated against the nominating digital service provider.
-- (4) is an official's power; (5) says "paragraph (1)" where the nomination is made under
-- paragraph (2). Both inert.

§ `Must I notify, and whom?`

-- src:153 | 1) The person specified in column 3 of the table in Schedule 1 is designated as the competent authority, for the territorial jurisdiction indicated in that column, and for the subsector specified in column 2 of that table (“the designated competent authorities”).
-- src:154 | 2) The Information Commission is designated as the competent authority for the United Kingdom for RDSPs.
-- src:285 | 1) An OES must notify the designated competent authority for the OES in writing about any incident which has a significant impact on the continuity of the essential service which that OES provides (“a network and information systems (“NIS”) incident”).
-- src:332 | 3) A RDSP must notify the Information Commission in writing about any incident having a substantial impact on the provision of any of the digital services mentioned in paragraph (1) that it provides.
-- src:333 | 4) The requirement to notify in paragraph (3) applies only if the RDSP has access to information which enables it to assess whether the impact of an incident is substantial.
-- src:353 | 9) If an OES is reliant on a RDSP to provide an essential service, the operator must notify the designated competent authority for the OES in writing in relation to it about any significant impact on the continuity of the service it provides caused by an incident affecting the RDSP without undue delay .
-- "Information Commission" is the text's word (Lex's 2026-09-30 text), where the 2018
-- text and the brief say "Information Commissioner" (finding in NOTES.md).
@ref regulation 3(1) and (2); regulations 11(1), 12(3) and 12(9) (src:153-154, src:285, src:332, src:353)
DECLARE `must I notify` IS ONE OF
    `I must notify`
    `I need not notify under these Regulations`
    `I must notify only if my service is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`

@ref regulation 3(1) and (2); regulations 11(1), 12(3) and 12(9) (src:153-154)
DECLARE `whom must I notify` IS ONE OF
    `the Information Commission and my designated competent authority`
    `the Information Commission`
    `my designated competent authority`
    `my designated competent authority; and the Information Commission too if my service is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`
    `the Information Commission, if my service is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`
    `no one under these Regulations`

@ref regulations 11(1) and 12(9) (src:285, src:353)
GIVEN p IS A `the provider as it describes itself`, e IS A `the event as I know it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I owe my designated competent authority a notification` p e IF
        `I must notify my designated competent authority under regulation 11(1)` p e
    OR  `I must notify my designated competent authority under regulation 12(9)` p e

@ref regulations 11(1), 12(3), 12(4) and 12(9) (src:285, src:332-333, src:353)
GIVEN p IS A `the provider as it describes itself`, e IS A `the event as I know it`
GIVETH A `must I notify`
`whether I must notify` p e MEANS
    IF `I owe my designated competent authority a notification` p e
        THEN `I must notify`
        ELSE CONSIDER `whether I must notify the Information Commission under regulation 12(3)` p e
             WHEN `the duty applies` THEN `I must notify`
             WHEN `the duty does not apply` THEN `I need not notify under these Regulations`
             WHEN `the duty applies only if my service is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`
                 THEN `I must notify only if my service is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`

@ref regulation 3(1) and (2); regulations 11(1), 12(3) and 12(9) (src:153-154, src:285, src:332, src:353)
GIVEN p IS A `the provider as it describes itself`, e IS A `the event as I know it`
GIVETH A `whom must I notify`
`whom I must notify` p e MEANS
    IF `I owe my designated competent authority a notification` p e
        THEN CONSIDER `whether I must notify the Information Commission under regulation 12(3)` p e
             WHEN `the duty applies` THEN `the Information Commission and my designated competent authority`
             WHEN `the duty does not apply` THEN `my designated competent authority`
             WHEN `the duty applies only if my service is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`
                 THEN `my designated competent authority; and the Information Commission too if my service is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`
        ELSE CONSIDER `whether I must notify the Information Commission under regulation 12(3)` p e
             WHEN `the duty applies` THEN `the Information Commission`
             WHEN `the duty does not apply` THEN `no one under these Regulations`
             WHEN `the duty applies only if my service is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`
                 THEN `the Information Commission, if my service is of a kind regulation 1 names, which I cannot say`

§ `By when? The 72-hour clocks of regulations 11(3)(b)(i) and 12(6)(a)`

-- src:299 | i) without undue delay and in any event no later than 72 hours after the operator is aware that a NIS incident has occurred; and
-- src:341 | 6) The notification under paragraph (3) must—
-- src:342 | a) be made without undue delay and in any event no later than 72 hours after the RDSP is first aware that an incident has occurred; and
-- src:343 | b) contain sufficient information to enable the Information Commission to determine the significance of any cross-border impact.
-- src:353 | 9) If an OES is reliant on a RDSP to provide an essential service, the operator must notify the designated competent authority for the OES in writing in relation to it about any significant impact on the continuity of the service it provides caused by an incident affecting the RDSP without undue delay .
-- Counting (fork F4): hours, not days. The clock starts at the moment of awareness the
-- provider states, and the last moment is exactly 72 hours (4,320 minutes) later; a
-- notice at 72h00m is "no later than 72 hours after", and at 72h01m it is late.
-- The Regulations name no time zone: both moments must be on one clock (e.g. UTC);
-- across a UK clock change, local wall-clock times would be an hour out.
-- "Without undue delay" may require notice sooner; the encoding gives only the outer
-- limit. Regulation 12(9) states no outer limit at all, so its answer is NOTHING.
@ref regulations 11(3)(b)(i), 12(6)(a) and 12(9) (src:299, src:341-343, src:353)
GIVEN m IS A `a moment`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the moment in minutes` m MEANS
    (Day (m's `day`) TIMES 1440) PLUS (m's `hour` TIMES 60) PLUS (m's `minute`)

@ref regulations 11(3)(b)(i) and 12(6)(a) (src:299, src:342)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`72 hours in minutes` MEANS 72 TIMES 60

@ref regulations 11(3)(b)(i), 12(6)(a) and 12(9) (src:299, src:342, src:353)
GIVEN d IS A `a notification duty`, aware IS A `a moment`
GIVETH A MAYBE `a moment`
`the last moment to notify under` d aware MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `regulation 12(9): an OES's notice of an incident affecting an RDSP it relies on` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST (`a moment` WITH
                        `day`    IS (aware's `day`) PLUS 3
                        `hour`   IS aware's `hour`
                        `minute` IS aware's `minute`)

@ref regulations 11(3)(b)(i), 12(6)(a) and 12(9) (src:299, src:342, src:353)
GIVEN d IS A `a notification duty`, aware IS A `a moment`, sent IS A `a moment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the notice was within the outer limit under` d aware sent MEANS
    CONSIDER d
    WHEN `regulation 12(9): an OES's notice of an incident affecting an RDSP it relies on` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST ((`the moment in minutes` sent MINUS `the moment in minutes` aware) AT MOST `72 hours in minutes`)

§ `Regulations 17 and 18 -- What can be done to me if I do not notify`

-- src:458 | Section 17) **Enforcement notices for breach of duties**
-- src:460 | 1) Subject to paragraph (2A), the designated competent authority for an OES may serve an enforcement notice upon that OES if the ... authority has reasonable grounds to believe that the OES has failed to—
-- src:463 | a) fulfil the security duties under regulation 10(1) and (2);
-- src:464 | b) notify a NIS incident under regulation 11(1);
-- src:465 | c) comply with the notification requirements stipulated in regulation 11(3);
-- src:466 | d) notify an incident as required by regulation 12(9);
-- src:471 | 2) Subject to paragraph (2A), the Information Commission may serve an enforcement notice upon a RDSP if the Information Commission has reasonable grounds to believe that the RDSP has failed to—
-- src:472 | a) fulfil its duties under regulation 12(1) or (2);
-- src:473 | b) notify an incident under regulation 12(3);
-- src:474 | c) comply with the notification requirements stipulated in regulation 12(5);
-- src:475 | d) comply with a direction made by the Information Commission under regulation 12(12);
-- Regulation 17(1)(c) names regulation 11(3), which holds the OES's 72-hour clock.
-- Regulation 17(2) names 12(3) and 12(5) but NOT 12(6), which holds the RDSP's 72-hour
-- clock (fork F3): on reading A a late notice is a failure to notify under 12(3); on
-- reading B lateness alone is not a failure 17(2) lists. Both are computed.
-- Regulation 12(9) has no 72-hour clock and no content list, so for that duty only a
-- failure to notify at all is answered here.
-- src:341 | 6) The notification under paragraph (3) must—
-- src:343 | b) contain sufficient information to enable the Information Commission to determine the significance of any cross-border impact.
-- A 12(6)(b) shortfall is not a 12(5) item either, so it takes the same two readings as
-- lateness; it binds only an RDSP.
@ref regulation 17(1)(a)-(d) and 17(2)(a)-(d) (src:458-475); regulation 12(6)(b) (src:341-343)
DECLARE `is the failure one regulation 17 lists in (a) to (d)` IS ONE OF
    `there was no failure`
    `yes, a failure regulation 17 lists in (a) to (d)`
    `no: on reading B, lateness alone is not a failure regulation 17(2) lists`
    `not answered here: regulation 12(9) sets no 72-hour clock and no list of contents`
    `no: on reading B, a regulation 12(6)(b) shortfall alone is not a failure regulation 17(2) lists`
    `not answered here: regulation 12(6)(b) binds only an RDSP`

@ref regulation 17(1)(b)-(d) and 17(2)(b)-(c); regulation 12(6)(b) (src:343)
GIVEN d IS A `a notification duty`, w IS A `what happened to my notification`, r IS A `a reading of late RDSP notice`
GIVETH A `is the failure one regulation 17 lists in (a) to (d)`
`whether my failure is one regulation 17 lists` d w r MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `I notified in time with the required information` THEN `there was no failure`
    WHEN `I did not notify at all` THEN `yes, a failure regulation 17 lists in (a) to (d)`
    WHEN `I notified, but more than 72 hours after the clock started` THEN
        CONSIDER d
        WHEN `regulation 11(1): an OES's NIS incident` THEN `yes, a failure regulation 17 lists in (a) to (d)`
        WHEN `regulation 12(9): an OES's notice of an incident affecting an RDSP it relies on` THEN `not answered here: regulation 12(9) sets no 72-hour clock and no list of contents`
        WHEN `regulation 12(3): an RDSP's incident` THEN
            CONSIDER r
            WHEN `reading A: a late notice is a failure to notify under regulation 12(3)` THEN `yes, a failure regulation 17 lists in (a) to (d)`
            WHEN `reading B: lateness alone is not a failure regulation 17(2) lists` THEN `no: on reading B, lateness alone is not a failure regulation 17(2) lists`
    WHEN `I notified in time, but without the required information` THEN
        CONSIDER d
        WHEN `regulation 12(9): an OES's notice of an incident affecting an RDSP it relies on` THEN `not answered here: regulation 12(9) sets no 72-hour clock and no list of contents`
        OTHERWISE `yes, a failure regulation 17 lists in (a) to (d)`
    WHEN `I notified in time with the regulation 12(5) items, but not enough for the Information Commission to determine the significance of any cross-border impact (regulation 12(6)(b))` THEN
        CONSIDER d
        WHEN `regulation 12(3): an RDSP's incident` THEN
            CONSIDER r
            WHEN `reading A: a late notice is a failure to notify under regulation 12(3)` THEN `yes, a failure regulation 17 lists in (a) to (d)`
            WHEN `reading B: lateness alone is not a failure regulation 17(2) lists` THEN `no: on reading B, a regulation 12(6)(b) shortfall alone is not a failure regulation 17(2) lists`
        OTHERWISE `not answered here: regulation 12(6)(b) binds only an RDSP`

-- src:532 | 7) In this regulation—
-- src:533 | a) “a material contravention” means—
-- src:534 | i) a failure to take, or adequately take, one or more of the steps required under an enforcement notice within the period specified in that notice to rectify a failure described in one or more of—
-- src:535 | aa) sub-paragraphs (a) to (d) of regulation 17(1); or
-- src:536 | bb) sub- paragraphs (a) to (d) of regulation 17(2); or
-- src:537 | ii) where an enforcement notice was not served or where no steps were required to be taken under an enforcement notice, a failure described in one or more of—
-- src:538 | aa) sub-paragraphs (a) to (d) of regulation 17(1); or
-- src:539 | bb) sub-paragraphs (a) to (d) of regulation 17(2).
-- Read literally, a listed failure for which an enforcement notice required steps that
-- WERE taken in time is neither (i) nor (ii), so it is not a material contravention
-- (fork F9). Regulation 18(6) gives "the NIS enforcement authority" the determination;
-- this computes what 18(7)(a) says from the facts.
@ref regulation 18(7)(a) (src:532-539)
GIVEN listed IS A `is the failure one regulation 17 lists in (a) to (d)`, n IS A `the enforcement notice position`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a material contravention` listed n IF
    CONSIDER listed
    WHEN `yes, a failure regulation 17 lists in (a) to (d)` THEN
        CONSIDER n
        WHEN `an enforcement notice required steps and I took them within its period` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:499 | Section 18) **Penalties**
-- src:501 | 1) The designated competent authority for an OES may serve a notice of intention to impose a penalty on the OES if it has reasonable grounds to believe that the OES has failed to comply with a duty referred to in regulation 17(1) or the duty set out in regulation 17(3A) and considers that a penalty is warranted having regard to the facts and circumstances of the case.
-- src:502 | 2) The Information Commission may serve a notice of intention to impose a penalty on a RDSP if it has reasonable grounds to believe that the RDSP has failed to comply with a duty referred to in regulation 17(2) or the duty set out in regulation (3A) and considers that a penalty is warranted having regard to the facts and circumstances of the case.
-- src:524 | 5) The sum of any penalty imposed under this regulation must be an amount that—
-- src:525 | a) the competent authority or Information Commission determines is appropriate and proportionate to the failure in respect of which it is imposed; and
-- src:526 | b) is in accordance with paragraph (6).
-- src:527 | 6) The amount ... must—
-- src:528 | a) not exceed £1,000,000 for any contravention which the NIS enforcement authority determines was not a material contravention ;
-- src:529 | b) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:530 | c) not exceed £8,500,000 for a material contravention which the NIS enforcement authority determines does not meet the criteria set out in sub-paragraph (d) ; and
-- src:531 | d) not exceed £17,000,000 for a material contravention which the NIS enforcement authority determines has or could have created a significant risk to, or significant impact on, or in relation to, the service provision by the OES or RDSP.
-- These are ceilings. Whether to impose a penalty at all, and the amount up to the
-- ceiling, are the authority's (18(1), (2), (5)(a); regulation 23); not encoded.
-- Regulation 18(2) reads "regulation (3A)", which is taken to mean 17(3A) (finding).
@ref regulation 18(1), (2), (5) and (6) (src:499-531)
DECLARE `the most I can be penalised` IS ONE OF
    `no penalty: there was no failure to notify`
    `no penalty under regulation 18 on reading B: lateness alone is not a failure regulation 17(2) lists`
    `not answered here: regulation 12(9) sets no 72-hour clock and no list of contents`
    `no penalty under regulation 18 on reading B: a regulation 12(6)(b) shortfall alone is not a failure regulation 17(2) lists`
    `not answered here: regulation 12(6)(b) binds only an RDSP`
    `up to 1,000,000 pounds: not a material contravention`
    `up to 8,500,000 pounds: a material contravention the authority determines does not meet regulation 18(6)(d)`
    `up to 17,000,000 pounds: a material contravention the authority determines has or could have created a significant risk to, or significant impact on, my service provision`
    `up to 8,500,000 pounds, or up to 17,000,000 pounds if the authority determines it has or could have created a significant risk to, or significant impact on, my service provision`

@ref regulation 18(6) (src:527-531); regulation 18(7)(a), quoted above
GIVEN d IS A `a notification duty`, w IS A `what happened to my notification`, r IS A `a reading of late RDSP notice`, n IS A `the enforcement notice position`, v IS A `the authority's view of the contravention`
GIVETH A `the most I can be penalised`
`the penalty ceiling for my failure to notify` d w r n v MEANS
    CONSIDER `whether my failure is one regulation 17 lists` d w r
    WHEN `there was no failure` THEN `no penalty: there was no failure to notify`
    WHEN `no: on reading B, lateness alone is not a failure regulation 17(2) lists` THEN `no penalty under regulation 18 on reading B: lateness alone is not a failure regulation 17(2) lists`
    WHEN `not answered here: regulation 12(9) sets no 72-hour clock and no list of contents` THEN `not answered here: regulation 12(9) sets no 72-hour clock and no list of contents`
    WHEN `no: on reading B, a regulation 12(6)(b) shortfall alone is not a failure regulation 17(2) lists` THEN `no penalty under regulation 18 on reading B: a regulation 12(6)(b) shortfall alone is not a failure regulation 17(2) lists`
    WHEN `not answered here: regulation 12(6)(b) binds only an RDSP` THEN `not answered here: regulation 12(6)(b) binds only an RDSP`
    WHEN `yes, a failure regulation 17 lists in (a) to (d)` THEN
        IF `it is a material contravention` `yes, a failure regulation 17 lists in (a) to (d)` n
            THEN CONSIDER v
                 WHEN `the authority determines it has or could have created a significant risk to, or significant impact on, my service provision`
                     THEN `up to 17,000,000 pounds: a material contravention the authority determines has or could have created a significant risk to, or significant impact on, my service provision`
                 WHEN `the authority determines it does not meet that test`
                     THEN `up to 8,500,000 pounds: a material contravention the authority determines does not meet regulation 18(6)(d)`
                 WHEN `the authority has not yet determined this`
                     THEN `up to 8,500,000 pounds, or up to 17,000,000 pounds if the authority determines it has or could have created a significant risk to, or significant impact on, my service provision`
            ELSE `up to 1,000,000 pounds: not a material contravention`

-- The highest figure each answer allows, in pounds; NOTHING where there is no penalty
-- or the question is not answered here.
@ref regulation 18(6) (src:527-531)
GIVEN c IS A `the most I can be penalised`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the ceiling in pounds` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `up to 1,000,000 pounds: not a material contravention` THEN JUST 1000000
    WHEN `up to 8,500,000 pounds: a material contravention the authority determines does not meet regulation 18(6)(d)` THEN JUST 8500000
    WHEN `up to 17,000,000 pounds: a material contravention the authority determines has or could have created a significant risk to, or significant impact on, my service provision` THEN JUST 17000000
    WHEN `up to 8,500,000 pounds, or up to 17,000,000 pounds if the authority determines it has or could have created a significant risk to, or significant impact on, my service provision` THEN JUST 17000000
    OTHERWISE NOTHING
